Do NOT generate any moat content \u2014 no headings, no recipes, no why text. This is a hard exclusion.\n- For COMPLEX_ENGINE software: If the provided context does not contain \"Quick Start\" or \"Settings\" guides, YOU MUST SEARCH for \"[software name] settings\", \"[software name] tips\", \"[software name] quick start guide\".\n- For COMPLEX_ENGINE software: Generate 2-3 practical settings recipes or quick-start steps that deliver real user value. NEVER pad with generic steps.\n\n4. WRITING STYLE:\n- YOU MUST FOLLOW THE EXACT SAME \"HUMAN WRITING STYLE\" (Sentence Variance, No Robotic Vocab, Syntax Variety) as defined for the regular mode.\n- The site voice must remain consistent across all posts.\n\n5. TAXONOMY:\n- Map the detected software to the `VALID_TAXONOMY_MAP` slugs.\n- FORMULA: You MUST select MULTIPLE categories. First, choose the supported Operating Systems. Then, choose the Software Type. Use SEARCH to verify categorization if unsure.\n\n6. CATEGORIZATION:\n- `category`: Return a comma-separated list of the selected category slugs.\n10. **FILE SIZE RULE**:\n- You MUST return only a single, clean value for `file_size` (e.g., '15.5 MB').\n- If multiple installers or platforms exist, pick the primary Windows installer size.\n- NEVER list multiple sizes or add parenthetical descriptions like '(online installer)' in the size field.\n\nRESEARCH MODE: Use Google Search to find the latest official information, changelogs, and download links. Do NOT invent data.\n\nSTATE: NEW POST. Create a comprehensive, high-quality software download post from scratch following the provided schema.\n\nCONTEXT \/ ARTICLE DATA:\nSource Context:\nSageThumbs 2K is the modern successor to the beloved SageThumbs project, bringing the same simple idea to today's versions of Windows with a completely refreshed foundation and vastly expanded format support. The lightweight Explorer extension enables Windows 10 and Windows 11 to display thumbnails for hundreds of file types that are not supported natively, including RAW camera images, PSD, HEIC, AVIF, JPEG XL (JXL), DDS, EXR, ebooks, comics, CAD, 3D assets, audio, and even many video formats. It integrates directly into File Explorer, making large collections of files easier to browse without opening dedicated applications.\n\nOriginally, SageThumbs became one of the most popular Windows shell extensions by giving File Explorer thumbnail previews for image formats that Windows could not display on its own. SageThumbs 2K builds on that legacy by preserving the familiar, lightweight experience while dramatically expanding compatibility with modern media formats and creative workflows. Whether you're organizing RAW photographs, previewing Photoshop PSD files, browsing HEIC images from smartphones, or managing AVIF, JPEG XL, DDS, EXR, and video files, Explorer becomes significantly more useful and productive.\n\nDesigned for speed, stability, and seamless Windows integration, SageThumbs 2K feels like a native part of File Explorer while eliminating the need to launch separate viewers just to identify files. With broad format support, fast thumbnail generation, and an actively modernized codebase, it revives the classic SageThumbs experience for a new generation of Windows users, photographers, designers, developers, and content creators.\n\nSageThumbs 2K 2.5.0 changelog highlights:\n\n\n    Optional sign-in reminders: Settings may now show a small suggestion to sign in with a Connections account so settings can be carried across multiple machines. The reminder is limited to once per day, can be dismissed, and signing in remains completely optional.\n    The installer now asks for this preference during a fresh installation, while upgrades preserve the previous configuration.\n    More reliable EPS thumbnails: More EPS files now display thumbnails because SageThumbs correctly handles files containing a blank line after the embedded preview header. EPS files without an embedded preview still cannot be rendered, since SageThumbs deliberately does not execute PostScript.\n    Correct Quick Preview tooltips: Button tooltips now dynamically reflect the action that will happen when clicked. This fixes incorrect descriptions for Light\/Dark mode, Pin, View Source, Mute, and Repeat buttons.\n    Improved plain-text email preview: Lines beginning with # in plain-text emails are no longer incorrectly interpreted as document headings. They now appear as normal text instead of being enlarged and added to the preview's outline. Quoted replies and numbered lists continue to be formatted correctly.\n\n\nNew thumbnail corner customization: \n\n\n    \nThe two confusing thumbnail-icon settings have been replaced with a single Appearance option. You can choose between:\n    Windows file-type icon \u2014 the default\n    SageThumbs format badge \u2014 e.g. PSD, JXL, AVIF\n    No icon\n\n\nPortable (no installer)\n\n\n    Extract and run. Nothing is installed, nothing goes in the registry, no admin needed. Settings live in SageThumbs2K.ini next to the exe.\n    It gives you the app and the command line tool: settings, convert and resize, quick preview, screenshots, OCR, the colour picker and the folder tools. It does not give you Explorer thumbnails or the right-click menu, because Windows only loads a shell extension whose COM class is registered. Install the normal build for those.\n\n\nDownload: SageThumbs 2K | Portable | ~20.0 MB (Open Source)\nDownload: ARM64 | Portable | ~20.0 MB (Open Source)\nLink: Home Page | Github | Screenshot\n\nSOURCE_URL: unknown\n\nPHP_DETECTED_METADATA (Weak Hints):\n{\"software_name\":\"SageThumbs 2K\",\"version\":\"2.5.0\",\"homepage\":\"https:\\\/\\\/sagethumbs2k.github.io\\\/\",\"category\":\"\",\"is_existing_article\":false,\"detected_version\":\"2.5.0\",\"detected_file_size\":\"20.0 MB\",\"resolved_links\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\\/\\\/github.com\\\/LunarWerxs\\\/SageThumbs-2k\\\/releases\\\/download\\\/v2.5.0\\\/SageThumbs2K-Setup-2.5.0-arm64.e